:"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gzb1128","html_url":"https://github.com/gzb1128","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gzb1128/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gzb1128/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gzb1128/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gzb1128/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gzb1128/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gzb1128/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gzb1128/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gzb1128/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gzb1128/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-09T12:13:07Z","updated_at":"2026-03-09T12:13:07Z","body":"@pohly Thank you for the thorough review! I've addressed all the feedback. I've updated test expectations in `pkg/scheduler/framework/plugins/dynamicresources/dynamicresources_test.go`. Tests now expect the complete error format including:\r\n       - Device ID (driver/pool/device)\r\n       - CEL optional chaining hint\r\n ## Example Error Messages\r\n\r\n  **CEL runtime error:**\r\n  class my-resource-class: selector #0 on device some-driver/worker/instance-1: CEL runtime error: no such key:\r\n  healthy. consider using CEL optional chaining (.? followed by orValue()) or guarding the check with has() for\r\n  optional fields\r\n\r\n  **Device conversion error:**\r\n  convert Device some-driver/worker/instance-1:\r\n\r\n  All unit tests are now passing. Ready for another review!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/comments/4023325024/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/comments/4140344665","html_url":"https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/pull/136709#issuecomment-4140344665","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/136709","id":4140344665,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAToIks72yKVZ","user":{"login":"gzb1128","id":55176411,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MTc2NDEx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55176411?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gzb1128","html_url":"https://github.com/gzb1128","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gzb1128/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gzb1128/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gzb1128/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gzb1128/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gzb1128/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gzb1128/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gzb1128/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gzb1128/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gzb1128/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-27T05:43:22Z","updated_at":"2026-03-27T05:43:22Z","body":"@pohly resolve some issue @troychiu mentioned . PTAL","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/comments/4140344665/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/comments/4196219287","html_url":"https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/pull/136709#issuecomment-4196219287","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/136709","id":4196219287,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAToIks76HTmX","user":{"login":"gzb1128","id":55176411,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MTc2NDEx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55176411?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gzb1128","html_url":"https://github.com/gzb1128","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gzb1128/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gzb1128/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gzb1128/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gzb1128/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gzb1128/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gzb1128/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gzb1128/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gzb1128/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gzb1128/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-07T03:07:27Z","updated_at":"2026-04-07T03:07:27Z","body":"@rajatchopra Thank you for the suggestion! This would indeed be a very nice enhancement.\r\n\r\nHowever, after investigating the cel-go library (v0.26.0), the \"no such key\" error doesn't expose a structured error type that we can use programmatically. There are two code paths that produce this error:\r\n\r\n1. **Attribute resolution path** (`interpreter/attributes.go`): There is a `resolutionError` struct with a `missingKey` field, but it is **unexported** — we cannot type-assert or access it from outside the `interpreter` package.\r\n2. **Map value path** (`common/types/map.go`): The key is baked into a `fmt.Errorf` format string with no structured data at all.\r\n\r\nBoth paths ultimately produce a `*types.Err` wrapping the error, but without a way to programmatically extract the missing key name. Implementing \"did you mean\" suggestions would require either:\r\n\r\n- Upstream changes to cel-go to export the error type or add a sentinel interface\r\n- Fragile string parsing of the error message, which would break if cel-go changes the format\r\n\r\nI'd suggest we track this as a future enhancement. We could file an issue against cel-go to request a programmatic way to inspect \"no such key\" errors, and then implement the suggestion feature once that's available. WDYT?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/comments/4196219287/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/comments/4207927767","html_url":"https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/pull/136709#issuecomment-4207927767","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/136709","id":4207927767,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAToIks76z-HX","user":{"login":"rajatchopra","id":982221,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk4MjIyMQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/982221?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajatchopra","html_url":"https://github.com/rajatchopra","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajatchopra/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajatchopra/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajatchopra/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajatchopra/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajatchopra/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajatchopra/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajatchopra/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajatchopra/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajatchopra/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-08T16:47:55Z","updated_at":"2026-04-08T16:47:55Z","body":"@gzb1128 Yes, this is an enhancement for cel-go. First get more information and then pass it with a more structured error format. Not a blocker for this 